WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.419
I was also watching the Olympics

00:00:02.419 --> 00:00:07.400
and I realized this when I was watching
the London Olympics

00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:11.900
and I was annoyed by how

00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:17.220
all the journalists asked all the athletes
the same stupid question

00:00:17.220 --> 00:00:18.982
literally, every one ...

00:00:18.982 --> 00:00:21.900
"Were you nervous?"

00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:23.769
or "Are you nervous?"

00:00:23.769 --> 00:00:25.200
whether it was before or after the event.

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:28.200
Every single time.

00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:31.080
And every single time all the athletes

00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:33.861
gave the exact same answer ...

00:00:33.861 --> 00:00:36.011
"No, I was excited."

00:00:36.011 --> 00:00:38.160
"No, I'm excited."

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:38.900
Every single time.

00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:41.340
These elite athletes had learned to interpret

00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:42.212
body stimulus ...

00:00:42.212 --> 00:00:44.379
what are the signs of nervousness?

00:00:44.379 --> 00:00:47.800
Your heart races, you visualize the future,
your hands get clammy.

00:00:47.800 --> 00:00:51.500
What are the stimulus for excitement?

00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:55.300
Your heart races, you visualize the future,
your hands get clammy.

00:00:55.300 --> 00:00:57.840
They had learned to interpret
what their body was telling them

00:00:57.840 --> 00:01:00.980
not as nerves
but as excitement.

00:01:00.980 --> 00:01:03.960
And the reason the journalists said, 
"Were you nervous?"

00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:07.960
is because they would be nervous.

00:01:07.960 --> 00:01:10.260
Athletes would never say that to each other.

00:01:10.260 --> 00:01:12.340
They'd say, "That was exciting!"

00:01:12.340 --> 00:01:16.470
So I tried it.
I did a little test on myself.

00:01:16.470 --> 00:01:20.540
I'm on a plane,
we start hitting some really bad turbulence.

00:01:20.540 --> 00:01:21.880
I go (gasp)

00:01:21.880 --> 00:01:24.300
and then I say to myself, 
literally out loud,

00:01:24.300 --> 00:01:27.560
"This is exciting!"

00:01:27.710 --> 00:01:31.520
And I was fine.

00:01:31.680 --> 00:01:33.000
And I was fine.

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:35.016
So I do it a lot now.

00:01:35.016 --> 00:01:38.940
When I find myself getting nervous
I say to myself,

00:01:38.940 --> 00:01:47.100
"This is so exciting" 
and I'll explain the reason to myself why.

00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:50.730
So, like an actor you don't get nervous
when you go on stage anymore

00:01:50.730 --> 00:01:51.895
but occasionally you do.

00:01:51.895 --> 00:01:54.900
So I get to go on stage a lot
and I don't really get nervous much anymore

00:01:54.900 --> 00:01:59.040
but I was going to
present to 3,000 chiefs of police

00:01:59.040 --> 00:02:06.150
right in the middle of all this police
brutality hullabaloo

00:02:06.150 --> 00:02:10.350
and I got really nervous because 
the stakes were really high

00:02:10.350 --> 00:02:15.660
and I was literally getting nervous backstage
and I said to myself,

00:02:15.660 --> 00:02:17.392
"This is so exciting.
I have an opportunity

00:02:17.392 --> 00:02:20.900
to talk to a group of people who can actually affect change in this country.

00:02:20.900 --> 00:02:23.380
This is really exciting."

00:02:23.380 --> 00:02:24.720
Now I could have said the same thing,

00:02:24.720 --> 00:02:27.206
"I'm so nervous,
I'm about to talk to people who could ... "

00:02:27.206 --> 00:02:29.200
but the interpretation was excitement.

00:02:29.200 --> 00:02:32.100
Just change the narrative.
It works brilliantly well.

